Spent 3 days optimizing Wan 2.1 on ComfyUI for consumer GPUs:

⚡ With SageAttention 2 and FP8 quantization, peak VRAM drops from 28GB to 13.8GB;
⚡ Runs smoothly on 16GB RTX 4080 / 4070Ti Super;
⚡ Integrated RIFE 4.25 frame interpolation outputs silky 60fps 4K video directly!

Free JSON workflow on GitHub, setup guide below👇

Sharing the latest production-grade 2026 AI video workflow on Threads:

Pure video models often suffer from facial drifting and clothing morphing across frames. After testing this week, the most reliable approach is the combo of 'Midjourney v7 Character Sheet + Seedance 2.5 Camera Rig':

1️⃣ Generate a 9-angle character reference sheet with fixed style tokens in Midjourney;
2️⃣ Feed the keyframe into Seedance 2.5, keeping the prompt focused strictly on camera motion (Pan, Tilt, Zoom) and ambient dynamics;
3️⃣ The native 4K 60fps output maintains over 95% character consistency across scene transitions!

Prompts and parameters shared in the thread below👇

Fastest way to run DeepSeek-R1 70B on a single 24GB GPU (RTX 3090/4090):

🔥 Ditch hybrid GGUF CPU offloading; use EXL2 3.25bpw precision quantization;
🔥 FlashInfer accelerates Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) kernels;
🔥 Time-to-first-token is 0.3s, sustained output reaches 52 tok/sec silently!

Docker commands and HuggingFace weights below👇

Dissecting ByteDance Seedance 2.5's most underrated feature on Threads—native audio-visual synchronization:

🎬 AI video has always been silent pantomime requiring manual sound design in post;
🎬 When Seedance 2.5 generates boots splashing in a puddle, frame 12 triggers the exact acoustic splash waveform;
🎬 When the camera glides inside a car, rain audio automatically applies natural low-pass filtering and cabin reverb!

